from (values
('113.46.c.11.A',3,'Ethnicity refers to what?','["Occupation", "A legal status", "Shared cultural heritage such as language, ancestry and traditions", "Only skin color"]'::jsonb,2,'Race is socially defined by physical traits.','original'),
('113.46.c.11.B',3,'Prejudice differs from discrimination because prejudice is what?','["A law, while discrimination is a custom", "An action, while discrimination is an attitude", "A fact, while discrimination is a belief", "An attitude, while discrimination is an action"]'::jsonb,3,'Attitude versus behavior.','original'),
('113.46.c.11.B',3,'Bias in sociology refers to what?','["A tendency to favor or disfavor something without fair consideration", "A group", "A law", "A scientific measurement"]'::jsonb,0,'Bias can be conscious or unconscious.','original'),
('113.46.c.11.C',3,'One ramification of stereotyping is what?','["Improved opportunity", "The self-fulfilling prophecy in which people act as they are expected to", "Greater understanding", "Reduced prejudice"]'::jsonb,1,'Expectations can shape behavior.','original'),
('113.46.c.11.C',3,'Stereotyping can harm society by doing what?','["Ending discrimination", "Eliminating differences", "Limiting opportunities and reinforcing inequality", "Increasing trust"]'::jsonb,2,'It justifies unequal treatment.','original'),
('113.46.c.11.D',3,'Which describes a pattern of treatment of minority groups, in which a group is kept apart by law or custom?','["Amalgamation", "Assimilation", "Pluralism", "Segregation"]'::jsonb,3,'Jim Crow laws enforced it.','original'),
('113.46.c.11.D',3,'Assimilation occurs when what happens?','["A minority group adopts the culture of the dominant group", "The group is separated", "The group is expelled", "The group is eliminated"]'::jsonb,0,'Immigrants often assimilate over generations.','original'),
('113.46.c.11.E',3,'Institutional racism is best illustrated by what?','["A personal belief", "Discriminatory policies built into laws or practices such as redlining", "A private preference", "One individual''s rude comment"]'::jsonb,1,'It operates through institutions.','original'),
('113.46.c.11.E',3,'Redlining was a practice that did what?','["Increased minority homeownership", "Banned segregation", "Denied loans and insurance to residents of certain neighborhoods based on race", "Equalized school funding"]'::jsonb,2,'It shaped wealth gaps.','original'),
('113.46.c.12.A',3,'Gender roles affect opportunities by doing what?','["Guaranteeing equal pay", "Ending discrimination", "Eliminating differences", "Shaping expectations about careers, education and household duties"]'::jsonb,3,'Roles have limited options.','original'),
('113.46.c.12.A',3,'The "glass ceiling" refers to what?','["Invisible barriers that keep women and minorities from top positions", "A tax policy", "A building material", "Actual window glass"]'::jsonb,0,'Promotion barriers are often informal.','original'),
('113.46.c.12.B',3,'An effect of an aging society is what?','["A younger workforce", "Increased demand for health care and retirement benefits", "Lower health spending", "Fewer retirees"]'::jsonb,1,'Policy must adapt.','original'),
('113.46.c.12.B',3,'Ageism is what?','["Respect for elders", "A retirement plan", "Prejudice or discrimination based on age", "A study of age"]'::jsonb,2,'It affects older workers.','original'),
('113.46.c.12.C',3,'Which factor often differs in health care between nations?','["Time zones", "The alphabet", "Temperature", "Whether the government pays for universal coverage"]'::jsonb,3,'Systems range from private to public.','original'),
('113.46.c.12.C',3,'People in low-income countries often face what health challenge?','["Limited access to doctors and clean water", "Abundant hospitals", "Excess specialists", "Universal insurance"]'::jsonb,0,'Access affects life expectancy.','original'),
('113.46.c.12.D',3,'Differences in health care in the United States are often linked to what?','["Favorite sport", "Income, insurance coverage and location", "Hair color", "Birth order"]'::jsonb,1,'Access is unequal.','original'),
('113.46.c.12.D',3,'Medicare in the United States primarily serves what group?','["Children only", "All adults", "Adults ages sixty-five and older", "Active military only"]'::jsonb,2,'Medicaid serves low-income people.','original'),
('113.46.c.13.A',3,'One function of the family is what?','["Building highways", "Enforcing federal law", "Printing money", "Socializing children"]'::jsonb,3,'Families teach norms and values.','original'),
('113.46.c.13.A',3,'Compared with a century ago, the American family has changed in that what is true?','["Smaller households and more dual-income families", "Larger households only", "No single-parent homes", "Fewer working mothers"]'::jsonb,0,'Family structures have diversified.','original'),
('113.46.c.13.B',3,'A nuclear family consists of what?','["A couple with no children by law", "Parents and their children living together", "Several generations in one house", "Only siblings"]'::jsonb,1,'Extended families include other relatives.','original'),
('113.46.c.13.B',3,'Monogamy is a marriage pattern in which a person has what?','["Many spouses by law", "Several spouses", "One spouse at a time", "No spouse"]'::jsonb,2,'It is the legal norm in the U.S.','original'),
('113.46.c.13.C',3,'One trend in American family life is what?','["Fewer divorces than ever", "Larger families", "Earlier marriage", "Later marriage and a rise in cohabitation"]'::jsonb,3,'Americans marry later than in the past.','original'),
('113.46.c.13.C',3,'Many families today need which support because of work demands?','["Child care", "Fewer schools", "Less income", "Longer vacations"]'::jsonb,0,'Dual-income households rely on it.','original'),
('113.46.c.13.D',3,'Which can disrupt family life?','["A vacation", "Divorce, death or unemployment", "A school holiday", "A birthday"]'::jsonb,1,'These events change roles and finances.','original'),
('113.46.c.13.D',3,'Domestic violence harms family life by doing what?','["Improving communication", "Strengthening bonds", "Creating fear and damaging trust and safety", "Reducing conflict"]'::jsonb,2,'Resources exist to help victims.','original'),
('113.46.c.14.A',3,'In a free enterprise system, what is true?','["Competition is banned", "Prices are set by the state", "The government owns all property", "Private individuals own most businesses and compete for profit"]'::jsonb,3,'Socialism emphasizes public ownership.','original'),
('113.46.c.14.A',3,'Socialism as an economic system emphasizes what?','["Collective or government ownership of major industries", "Barter only", "No government role", "Unlimited private ownership"]'::jsonb,0,'It aims to reduce inequality.','original'),
('113.46.c.14.B',3,'A democracy is a government in which what is true?','["The military controls everything", "Power rests with the people, who choose leaders in elections", "One ruler holds absolute power", "A few elites rule by birth"]'::jsonb,1,'Legitimacy comes from consent.','original'),
('113.46.c.14.B',3,'Max Weber''s idea of legitimate authority includes which type?','["Authority from force alone", "Authority from wealth only", "Charismatic authority based on personal qualities of a leader", "Authority from age only"]'::jsonb,2,'Traditional and legal-rational are the others.','original'),
('113.46.c.14.C',3,'The right to vote in the United States has expanded over time to include what?','["Only men", "Only landowners", "Only the wealthy", "Women, African American men and eighteen-year-olds"]'::jsonb,3,'Amendments extended suffrage.','original'),
('113.46.c.14.C',3,'The Nineteenth Amendment is significant because it did what?','["Gave women the right to vote", "Lowered the voting age", "Ended poll taxes", "Abolished slavery"]'::jsonb,0,'Ratified in 1920.','original'),
('113.46.c.15.A',3,'The functionalist theory of education says schools do what?','["Create conflict only", "Transmit culture and prepare people for roles in society", "Are unnecessary", "Maintain class inequality only"]'::jsonb,1,'Education serves society''s needs.','original'),
('113.46.c.15.A',3,'Conflict theorists argue that education does what?','["Eliminates inequality", "Is always fair", "Reproduces social inequality through tracking and unequal funding", "Has no effect"]'::jsonb,2,'Funding disparities matter.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Social Studies' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
